# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/kit/shops.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event shop_square
# en: Market Day
title [0bcdaf] = 集市日
# en: {The square is all stalls today, with the bakery's trestle, the tailor's rail of robes, the pawnbroker's sign creaking over his door.|Market day again. The baker's girl is shouting the price of buns as if it were news.|The tailor has put a new robe in the window and is standing behind it, watching people's faces.} {met(mir): {Mir has a stall by the well, under a sign that says WANDS, IMPROVED (PROBABLY).|Mir's stall has grown a canopy and a small, worried sign: PLEASE DO NOT TEST ON THE BAKERY.|Mir is at the stall, rewinding something that should not need rewinding.}|{A pigeon is eating the display.|Somebody is haggling over a cabbage with real feeling.|A barge horn sounds from the jetty.}}
text [190a3d] = {今天广场上全是摊子：烘焙坊的支架桌，裁缝的长袍衣架，当铺门上吱呀作响的招牌。|又是集市日。烘焙坊的姑娘大声报着面包的价钱，好像那是什么新闻。|裁缝在橱窗里挂了一件新袍子，自己站在后面，看路人的表情。} {met(mir): {米尔在井边摆了个摊，招牌上写着：魔杖，改良版（大概）。|米尔的摊子多了个顶棚，还有一块忧心忡忡的小牌子：请勿对着烘焙坊试杖。|米尔在摊子上，正给一样本不该需要上发条的东西上发条。}|{一只鸽子在啄摊上的货。|有人正满怀激情地为一棵卷心菜讨价还价。|码头传来驳船的汽笛声。}}
# en: A cobbled market square, a bakery stall steaming, a tailor's window full of robes, a pawnbroker's sign and a student's stall of odd wands.
scene [6a4545] = 铺着鹅卵石的集市广场，烘焙坊的摊子冒着热气，裁缝的橱窗挂满长袍，当铺挂着招牌，还有一个学生摆的古怪魔杖摊。
# en: A bag of warm buns
opt.buns.label [5281f2] = 一袋热面包
# en: A little Health.
opt.buns.hint [f30bb0] = 少许健康。
# en: {The buns are still hot enough to hurt. You eat two on the walk back and save one, nearly.|The baker's girl throws in a crooked one for free. It's the best of the lot.|Sugar on your fingers, sugar on your robes. Worth it.}
opt.buns.say.1 [fa67ed] = {面包还烫得能伤人。回去路上你吃了两个，差点留下了一个。|烘焙坊的姑娘白送你一个歪的。那是最好吃的一个。|手指上是糖，袍子上也是糖。值了。}
# en: The quilted duelling coat
opt.coat.label [a636dd] = 绗缝决斗外套
# en: A robe for fights: more Health, and Brace costs less.
opt.coat.hint [82d4d4] = 战斗用长袍：更多生命，坚守更省。
# en: {The tailor buttons you into it and thumps you on the chest. "There. Now you're a wall."|It's heavier than it looks and smells faintly of the duelling hall. You feel braver at once, which may be the padding.|"Singed in the duelling hall? Bring it back and I'll patch it," says the tailor, which is not reassuring.}
opt.coat.say.1 [da3dcb] = {裁缝替你扣好扣子，在你胸口拍了一下。“好了。现在你是一堵墙。”|它比看上去重，隐约有决斗厅的味道。你立刻觉得勇敢了些，也许只是因为垫得厚。|“在决斗厅烧坏了？拿回来我给你补，”裁缝说。这话并不让人安心。}
# en: The duelling coat, at the Circle's price
opt.coat_circle.label [0134d6] = 决斗外套，决斗社价
# en: A robe for fights: more Health, and Brace costs less.
opt.coat_circle.hint [82d4d4] = 战斗用长袍：更多生命，坚守更省。
# en: {"Circle members pay what the Circle pays," says the tailor, and charges you half. "Don't tell the others."|The tailor knows the Circle's crest and knocks the price down without being asked.|"Half price for the Circle. Your captain sent three of you last week. Two came back singed."}
opt.coat_circle.say.1 [30228c] = {“决斗社的人，照决斗社的价，”裁缝说，只收了你一半。“别告诉别人。”|裁缝认得决斗社的徽章，没等你开口就把价钱降了下来。|“决斗社半价。你们社长上周送来三个，回去两个被烧焦了。”}
# en: Midnight-blue robes
opt.robes.label [528263] = 午夜蓝长袍
# en: A good robe: a little more Health in a fight, and people stand up straighter.
opt.robes.hint [e2baf5] = 好长袍：战斗中多一点生命，别人见了也会挺直腰板。
# en: {Deep blue wool, silver at the hem, a lining like the night sky. In the tailor's mirror you look like someone in a portrait.|The tailor pins the hem with her mouth full of pins and still manages to say "Lovely".|It costs more than you meant to spend. It also fits as if it had been waiting for you.}
opt.robes.say.1 [02b645] = {深蓝羊毛，镶着银边，里衬像夜空。在裁缝的镜子里，你像肖像画里的人。|裁缝嘴里含满大头针给你别下摆，居然还能说出一句“真好看”。|它比你打算花的钱多。可它合身得好像一直在等你。}
# en: Midnight-blue robes, for your old ones
opt.robes_swap.label [e96b29] = 午夜蓝长袍，以旧换新
# en: Bring the robes you bought before; the tailor takes them off your hands at half price.
opt.robes_swap.hint [d691f6] = 带上你以前买的长袍，裁缝半价收走。
# en: {"Stained at the Ball? Bring them here." The tailor takes your old robes, sniffs them, and fits you properly at half price.|She holds your old robes up to the light, tuts at a stain, and takes them off your hands. The new ones are the same blue, properly cut.|"Half price for the old ones back. I'll turn them into cushions." You don't ask whose cushions.}
opt.robes_swap.say.1 [9c9403] = {“在舞会上弄脏了？拿到这儿来。”裁缝收下你的旧袍子，闻了闻，半价给你重新量体裁衣。|她把旧袍子举到亮处，对着一块污渍啧啧两声，收下了。新的同样是深蓝，剪裁得体。|“旧的交回来，半价。我拿它们做靠垫。”你没问是谁的靠垫。}
# en: A hazelwood wand from Mir's stall
opt.hazel.label [19f1f9] = 米尔摊上的榛木魔杖
# en: A light, quick wand: a little more Mana in a fight.
opt.hazel.hint [4bbe94] = 轻巧灵敏的魔杖：战斗中多一点法力。
# en: {Mir wraps it in a page of their own notes. "This one likes to be used. Probably."|"I re-cored it twice," Mir says. "The second time on purpose."|Mir waves it once over the stall and a cabbage rolls politely out of the way. "See? Improved."}
opt.hazel.say.1 [fc6781] = {米尔用一页自己的笔记把它包好。“这根喜欢被用。大概吧。”|“我给它换了两次杖芯，”米尔说，“第二次是故意的。”|米尔在摊子上方挥了一下，一棵卷心菜很有礼貌地滚开了。“看到没？改良版。”}
# en: Trade the borrowed wand to Mir for hazel
opt.hazel_swap.label [8c9fa8] = 把借来的魔杖换成榛木的
# en: Mir takes the academy's loaner in part-exchange: a little more Mana in a fight.
opt.hazel_swap.hint [64cd5e] = 米尔收下学院的借用杖抵一部分钱：战斗中多一点法力。
# en: {"That borrowed wand's held together with hope," says Mir, taking it gently. "I'll give it a better one. Hope, I mean."|Mir weighs the old wand, winces at the chipped tip and hands you a hazel one, warm from the sun.|"I'll fix this one up for next year's first-years," Mir says. "Someone will need it. Probably you, in spirit."}
opt.hazel_swap.say.1 [1540fa] = {“这根借来的魔杖全靠希望撑着，”米尔小心地接过去，“我给它换个更好的。我是说，换个更好的希望。”|米尔掂了掂旧魔杖，看到崩掉的杖尖皱了皱眉，递给你一根晒得暖烘烘的榛木杖。|“我把这根修好，留给明年的一年级生，”米尔说，“总会有人需要它的。精神上大概就是你。”}
# en: Sell something at the pawnbroker's
opt.pawn.label [8103da] = 去当铺卖点东西
# en: He buys what you no longer want, at less than you paid.
opt.pawn.hint [f6ae90] = 他收你不再想要的东西，价钱比你买时低。
# en: {The pawnbroker's bell rings like a sigh.|The stuffed owl in his window watches you go in.|"Ah," says the pawnbroker, who says "ah" to everyone.}
opt.pawn.say.1 [882f26] = {当铺的门铃响得像一声叹息。|他橱窗里那只猫头鹰标本目送你进门。|“啊，”当铺老板说。他对谁都说“啊”。}
# en: Just looking
opt.look.label [4af612] = 随便看看
# en: {You walk the stalls with your hands in your pockets. The smell of the bakery is free.|You admire the tailor's window from a safe, inexpensive distance.|You buy nothing and enjoy the noise. Market days are good for that.}
opt.look.say.1 [55200c] = {你双手插兜在摊子间闲逛。烘焙坊的香味不要钱。|你在安全、不花钱的距离外欣赏裁缝的橱窗。|你什么也没买，享受着热闹。集市日就适合这样。}

@event shop_pawn
# en: The Pawnbroker's Counter
title [d08e15] = 当铺柜台
# en: {The pawnbroker turns each thing over twice, as if it might be hiding a second, cheaper thing underneath.|"Ah," says the pawnbroker, screwing in his loupe. "Let's see what you're tired of."|Behind him, the stuffed owl. In front of him, a ledger. Neither looks sentimental.} He pays fair, he says, for what is no longer loved.
text [2de4e7] = {当铺老板把每样东西都翻过来看两遍，好像底下还藏着一样更便宜的东西。|“啊，”当铺老板说着，把放大镜拧进眼眶，“看看你厌倦了什么。”|他身后是猫头鹰标本，身前是账本。两样看起来都不念旧。}他说，不再被珍爱的东西，他都给公道价。
# en: A narrow shop crammed with other people's treasures, a stuffed owl on a shelf and a pawnbroker with a loupe in one eye.
scene [7a09a8] = 一间塞满别人宝贝的窄小铺子，架子上一只猫头鹰标本，老板一只眼睛夹着放大镜。
# en: The hazelwood wand
opt.hazel.label [2c3297] = 榛木魔杖
# en: He tests it on a candle and nods. "Light. Some student will like it."
opt.hazel.say.1 [781493] = 他拿它在蜡烛上试了试，点点头。“轻。会有学生喜欢的。”
# en: The ashwood duelling wand
opt.ashwood.label [eb833d] = 白蜡木决斗魔杖
# en: He holds it at arm's length, as if it might bite. "Duellists come in here sometimes. Usually limping."
opt.ashwood.say.1 [766c04] = 他把它拿得远远的，好像它会咬人。“决斗的人有时会来这儿。通常是瘸着来的。”
# en: The heartwood wand
opt.heartwood.label [5ee7b9] = 心材魔杖
# en: He goes quiet over the grain. "That's not from any wood I sell." He pays well. You feel it go, the whole way home.
opt.heartwood.say.1 [6b250c] = 他对着木纹沉默了。“这不是我卖过的任何一种木头。”他出价很高。回去的一路上，你都能感觉到它不在了。
# en: The quilted duelling coat
opt.coat.label [a636dd] = 绗缝决斗外套
# en: He pokes a finger through a singed patch and docks the price for it.
opt.coat.say.1 [f311c3] = 他用手指戳了戳一块烧焦的地方，为此压了价。
# en: The ward-stitched cloak
opt.cloak.label [5947b9] = 护界绣斗篷
# en: He holds the hem to the lamp and the ward thread flickers. "Sister Amaranth's work. I'll keep it out of the window."
opt.cloak.say.1 [10b531] = 他把下摆凑到灯下，护界线闪了一下。“阿玛兰斯修女的手艺。这件我不放橱窗。”
# en: The midnight-blue robes
opt.robes.label [7b2814] = 午夜蓝长袍
# en: "Lovely cut," he says, and pays you a third of it.
opt.robes.say.1 [8867b8] = “剪裁真好，”他说，然后只付了三分之一的价。
# en: The Spinner-silk robe
opt.silk.label [b79365] = 织网者丝袍
# en: He touches the silk and takes his hand back very quickly. Then he pays, a great deal, without haggling.
opt.silk.say.1 [ec28ba] = 他碰了碰丝绸，飞快地把手缩了回去。然后一分没还价，付了一大笔钱。
# en: The lodestone pendant
opt.lodestone.label [c54545] = 磁石吊坠
# en: He sets it on the counter and it turns, slowly, to the north wall. "Huh," he says, and pays.
opt.lodestone.say.1 [83070b] = 他把它放在柜台上，它慢慢转向了北面的墙。“嗯，”他说，付了钱。
# en: The stag's tine
opt.tine.label [3d2dbd] = 鹿角尖
# en: He doesn't ask where you got it. The stuffed owl seems to.
opt.tine.say.1 [e479c6] = 他没问你从哪儿弄来的。猫头鹰标本好像想问。
# en: The owl-feather quill
opt.quill.label [2cd309] = 猫头鹰羽毛笔
# en: "A quill's a quill," he says. It writes "a quill's a quill" on his ledger by itself, and he pays a little more.
opt.quill.say.1 [e7172a] = “笔就是笔，”他说。笔自己在他账本上写下“笔就是笔”，他多付了一点。
# en: The moonpetal locket
opt.locket.label [4a8f97] = 月瓣吊盒
# en: He opens it, sees the petal, closes it again. "Pretty," he says. It's the kindest word he's used all day.
opt.locket.say.1 [ec6625] = 他打开，看见那片花瓣，又合上。“好看，”他说。这是他今天说过最温柔的一个词。
# en: The pocket almanac
opt.almanac.label [3082b1] = 袖珍年历
# en: He flicks through Grimsby's pencil notes and snorts. "He'll buy it back off me by Tuesday."
opt.almanac.say.1 [307c53] = 他翻了翻格林斯比的铅笔批注，哼了一声。“不出星期二，他就会从我这儿买回去。”
# en: Pell's measuring spoon
opt.spoon.label [ad193a] = 佩尔的量勺
# en: "Brass," he says, "worn thin." He pays for the brass.
opt.spoon.say.1 [68a601] = “黄铜，”他说，“磨薄了。”他按黄铜的价付钱。
# en: The honey tin
opt.honey.label [3d60fc] = 蜂蜜罐
# en: He shakes it, sniffs it and pays a few coins. A silver bee follows you all the way to the jetty, looking disappointed.
opt.honey.say.1 [cb7a66] = 他摇了摇，闻了闻，给了几个硬币。一只银蜂一路跟你到码头，看上去很失望。
# en: Keep it all
opt.keep.label [dce93a] = 都留着吧
# en: {You put everything back in your bag. The pawnbroker shrugs. "Ah."|Not today. The owl watches you go.|You find you're fond of it all after all.}
opt.keep.say.1 [d1a8fd] = {你把东西全放回包里。当铺老板耸耸肩。“啊。”|今天不卖了。猫头鹰目送你离开。|你发现自己还是舍不得这些东西。}

@event shop_mabels
# en: Mabel's Counter
title [160cd0] = 梅布尔的柜台
# en: {Mabel looks at you once as you come in and is already reaching for a tin. "Sit, petal. I know what you want; let's see if you do."|"There's my petal," says Mabel. "You've the look of someone who needs something steeped."|The bell over the door. Mabel doesn't turn round. "Ginger, by the sound of that door," she says.} {The courage blend is in the green tin; the calm blend in the blue.|A sign on the counter reads: TONICS — ONE AT A TIME. MABEL.|The cups on the hooks behind her catch the light.}
text [3e1a8b] = {你一进门，梅布尔看了你一眼，已经伸手去拿茶罐了。“坐吧，小花瓣。我知道你要什么，看看你自己知不知道。”|“我的小花瓣来了，”梅布尔说，“你一脸需要泡点什么的样子。”|门铃响了。梅布尔没回头。“听这开门声，是要姜茶，”她说。} {勇气茶在绿罐子里，安神茶在蓝罐子里。|柜台上的牌子写着：补剂——一次一种。梅布尔。|她身后挂钩上的茶杯闪着光。}
# en: A small warm tea shop with forty tins on the shelves, three cakes under glass and a woman behind the counter already reaching for a pot.
scene [a2659a] = 一间温暖的小茶馆，架上四十个茶罐，玻璃罩下三种蛋糕，柜台后的女人已经伸手去拿茶壶了。
# en: A pot of tea
opt.tea.label [3591b6] = 一壶茶
# en: A little Mood.
opt.tea.hint [26b71f] = 少许心情。
# en: {She brings it before you've sat down. It's exactly right, which is worrying.|A pot, a cup and a slice of cake you didn't order and don't pay for. "Crumbs," she says. "Day-old."|You drink it by the window and watch the barge come in. The day gets a little easier.}
opt.tea.say.1 [4ee98a] = {你还没坐下她就端来了。正合你意，这让人有点担心。|一壶茶，一个杯子，还有一块你没点、也不用付钱的蛋糕。“边角料，”她说，“隔夜的。”|你坐在窗边喝茶，看驳船靠岸。这一天好过了一点。}
# en: The courage blend
opt.courage.label [196e93] = 勇气茶
# en: A tonic for a month: asking for things and performing come easier.
opt.courage.hint [92b427] = 一个月的补剂：开口求人和登台表演更容易。
# en: {"Ginger, honey and something I don't tell," says Mabel, screwing the lid on. "One cup a morning. Speak up, petal."|She weighs it out on her little scales. "For the nerve," she says. "Not for being rude. Different tin."|You drink a cup there and then. Your voice comes out a size bigger when you thank her.}
opt.courage.say.1 [af18e1] = {“姜、蜂蜜，还有一样我不说的，”梅布尔拧上盖子，“每天早上一杯。大声说话，小花瓣。”|她在小秤上称好。“是给胆子用的，”她说，“不是给你没礼貌用的。那是另一罐。”|你当场喝了一杯。道谢时，你的声音大了一号。}
# en: The calm blend
opt.calm.label [420ab8] = 安神茶
# en: A tonic for a month: exams and frightened animals come easier.
opt.calm.hint [b400aa] = 一个月的补剂：考试和安抚受惊的动物更容易。
# en: {"Chamomile, lavender, a pinch of moonwort," says Mabel. "For exams. And for your hands, petal. They're shaking."|She hands you the blue tin. "Breathe before you open the paper. The tea only does half."|"Good for nerves and nervous beasts," says Mabel. "Don't ask me why. It just is."}
opt.calm.say.1 [7990cf] = {“洋甘菊、薰衣草，一小撮月草，”梅布尔说，“考试用的。还有你的手，小花瓣。它们在抖。”|她递给你蓝罐子。“翻开试卷前先深呼吸。茶只管一半。”|“对紧张的人和紧张的牲口都管用，”梅布尔说，“别问我为什么。就是管用。”}
# en: Just say hello
opt.chat.label [781d00] = 只是打个招呼
# en: {Mabel tells you three things about the village and one about yourself. The last one is right.|You lean on the counter and let her talk. It costs nothing and helps more than tea.|"Off you go, then," she says, "and come back with better news."}
opt.chat.say.1 [c092cb] = {梅布尔告诉你三件村里的事，一件关于你的事。最后一件说对了。|你靠在柜台上听她说话。不花钱，比茶还管用。|“去吧，”她说，“下次带好消息来。”}

@event shop_grimsbys
# en: Grimsby's Counter
title [f5d1f8] = 格林斯比的柜台
# en: {Mr Grimsby is up a ladder, sniffing a spine. "Ah! Not that one," he says, and hands you a different one.|Grimsby greets you like an old customer, by the title of a book you've never read. He has no idea what you came in for today.|The shop smells of dust and pipe smoke and one shelf, somewhere, of the sea.} {A stack of exam primers leans on the counter like a tired student.|A box by the door says BOOKS BOUGHT BACK, FAIR PRICES, NO QUESTIONS (SOME QUESTIONS).|A lighthouse print hangs crooked behind the till.}
text [149f00] = {格林斯比先生爬在梯子上，闻着一本书的书脊。“啊！不是这本，”他说，递给你另一本。|格林斯比像招呼老主顾一样跟你打招呼，报的却是一本你从没读过的书名。他完全不知道你今天来买什么。|店里有灰尘和烟斗的味道，某个书架上，还有大海的味道。} {一摞备考手册靠在柜台上，像个累坏了的学生。|门边的箱子上写着：旧书回收，价钱公道，不问问题（问几个）。|收银台后面歪挂着一幅灯塔版画。}
# en: A bookshop crowded to the rafters, shelves leaning on each other, an old man in half-moon glasses sniffing the spine of a book.
scene [ebe92b] = 一家书塞到房梁的书店，书架互相倚靠，戴半月形眼镜的老人正闻着一本书的书脊。
# en: Let him choose you a book
opt.pick.label [99cfbe] = 让他替你挑本书
# en: Skill XP, in whatever he thinks you need.
opt.pick.hint [fd7e6c] = 技能经验，他觉得你缺什么就给什么。
# en: He sniffs three books and hands you the fourth. It's on a subject you'd never have picked, and you can't put it down.
opt.pick.say.1 [3f2faa] = 他闻了三本书，递给你第四本。那个题目你从来不会选，可你放不下了。
# en: "This one," he says, holding out a battered spellbook. "It smells of thunder." It does, and it's very good.
opt.pick.say.2 [1e30df] = “这本，”他说着递来一本破旧的咒语书，“它有雷雨的味道。”确实有，而且写得很好。
# en: He gives you a herbal with someone's pressed flowers still inside. "The flowers were extra. I mean free. I mean extra."
opt.pick.say.3 [c9b692] = 他给你一本草药志，里面还夹着别人压的花。“花是额外的。我是说免费的。我是说额外的。”
# en: An exam primer
opt.primer.label [682108] = 一本备考手册
# en: A little exam preparation for every course you're taking.
opt.primer.hint [981bc2] = 你修的每门课都多一点考试准备。
# en: {The primer is dog-eared in all the right places. Someone passed with this book before you.|Grimsby hands it over reluctantly. "Exams," he says, as if naming a sad illness.|You read the first chapter on the barge home and, for once, the questions look like ones you could answer.}
opt.primer.say.1 [cd438e] = {手册在恰当的地方都折了角。在你之前，有人靠这本书考过了。|格林斯比不太情愿地递过来。“考试，”他说，好像在说一种令人难过的病。|你在回去的驳船上读了第一章，难得地，那些题目看起来你能答。}
# en: Sell a book back
opt.sell.label [8e49b6] = 卖回一本书
# en: A few crowns, and a book fewer.
opt.sell.hint [629956] = 几个克朗，少一本书。
# en: {He pays for it and puts it on a shelf you'll never find again. You miss it at once.|"Fair price," he says, and it is. You miss the book anyway.|He sniffs it, approves, and pays. Your shelf at the castle looks a little emptier tonight.}
opt.sell.say.1 [8a09ca] = {他付了钱，把书放到一个你再也找不到的架子上。你立刻就想它了。|“公道价，”他说，确实公道。你还是会想那本书。|他闻了闻，满意地付了钱。今晚城堡里你的书架看起来空了一点。}
# en: Browse the shelves
opt.browse.label [9177cc] = 逛逛书架
# en: {You spend an hour reading the first pages of twenty books. It's the best hour of the week.|You find a book you want and can't afford, and read a chapter of it standing up.|Grimsby recommends a book by its smell. You leave with nothing and an appetite.}
opt.browse.say.1 [2168b2] = {你花一个小时读了二十本书的开头几页。这是一周里最好的一个小时。|你找到一本想要却买不起的书，站着读完了一章。|格林斯比凭气味给你推荐书。你空手而归，胃口大开。}

@event shop_pell
# en: Pell's Counter
title [3574ec] = 佩尔的柜台
# en: {One of Pell's daughters is at the counter. Behind her, Old Pell counts drops aloud and doesn't look up.|"Tonic or draught?" asks the daughter on the counter. "Dad will say draught. Dad always says draught."|The drawers rattle as you come in, as if they were sorting themselves.} {A card on the till reads MEASURED TWICE, SOLD ONCE.|Old Pell is arguing with a label.|The smell of mint and something sterner.}
text [8e1a84] = {佩尔的一个女儿在柜台。她身后，老佩尔大声数着药滴，头也不抬。|“补剂还是药剂？”柜台后的女儿问，“爸爸会说药剂。爸爸总说药剂。”|你一进门，抽屉们就咔嗒作响，好像在自己整理。} {收银台上的卡片写着：量两遍，卖一次。|老佩尔在跟一张标签争论。|薄荷味，还有一种更严肃的味道。}
# en: An apothecary of a thousand labelled drawers, a daughter behind the counter, an old man counting drops at the back.
scene [22b99b] = 一家有上千个贴着标签的抽屉的药铺，柜台后站着一个女儿，后面一个老人在数药滴。
# en: Pell's tonic
opt.tonic.label [6e083d] = 佩尔的补剂
# en: A little Health.
opt.tonic.hint [f30bb0] = 少许健康。
# en: {It tastes of mint and iron. Halfway back to the castle you realise you've stopped yawning.|The daughter pours it; Pell checks the measure from across the room. "Right," he says. It is.|"Two spoons at bedtime," says the daughter. "Not three. Dad will know."}
opt.tonic.say.1 [8918b7] = {有薄荷和铁的味道。回城堡走到一半，你发现自己不打哈欠了。|女儿倒药，佩尔隔着屋子检查分量。“对了，”他说。确实对了。|“睡前两勺，”女儿说，“别三勺。爸爸会知道的。”}
# en: The steadying draught
opt.draught.label [a644e3] = 定神药剂
# en: A tonic for a month: research, brewing and enchanting come easier.
opt.draught.hint [266879] = 一个月的补剂：研究、调制和附魔更容易。
# en: {Old Pell measures it himself, counting aloud. "Steady hands," he says. "That's all it does. That's all anyone needs."|The draught tastes of nothing at all, which the daughter says is the expensive part.|"For the fine work," says Pell, corking it. "Don't waste it on the coarse work."}
opt.draught.say.1 [e6d447] = {老佩尔亲自量，一边大声数着。“手要稳，”他说，“它就管这个。人人需要的也就这个。”|这药剂什么味道都没有，女儿说这就是贵的地方。|“做精细活用的，”佩尔塞上瓶塞，“别浪费在粗活上。”}
# en: Just looking
opt.look.label [4af612] = 随便看看
# en: {You read labels until the daughter asks if you're lost. You are, a little.|You leave with nothing but the smell of mint in your robes.|Pell glances up once, decides you're not buying, and goes back to his drops.}
opt.look.say.1 [dac02a] = {你读标签读到女儿问你是不是迷路了。你确实有点迷路。|你什么也没买，只带走了袍子上的薄荷味。|佩尔抬头看了一眼，断定你不买，又低头去数他的药滴。}

@event shop_newt
# en: The Newt's Counter
title [aa46a0] = 蝾螈酒馆的吧台
# en: {{slot == "afternoon": By day the Gilded Newt is quiet, just a fire, a few regulars and the landlady with a cloth over her shoulder.|At this hour the Gilded Newt is all elbows and cider, and the landlady works the bar with a cloth over her shoulder.}|{slot == "afternoon": The Newt in the afternoon smells of bread and last night's cider. Someone is asleep by the fire.|The Newt smells of cider and wet coats tonight. Someone is singing by the fire, badly.}|The landlady nods at you over the bar. "Supper's on. Cider's cold. Table's free."} {The slate says HOT SUPPER, A ROUND, CIDER.|A cat is asleep in the bread basket.|A barge crew is arguing about weather.}
text [438b30] = {{slot == "afternoon": 白天的镀金蝾螈很安静，只有炉火、几个常客，和肩上搭着抹布的老板娘。|这个钟点的镀金蝾螈挤满了胳膊肘和苹果酒，老板娘肩上搭着抹布在吧台后忙活。}|{slot == "afternoon": 午后的蝾螈有面包和昨晚苹果酒的味道。有人在炉火边睡着了。|今晚的蝾螈有苹果酒和湿外套的味道。有人在炉火边唱歌，唱得很糟。}|老板娘隔着吧台冲你点点头。“晚饭好了。苹果酒是凉的。桌子空着。”} {石板上写着：热晚饭、请一轮、苹果酒。|一只猫睡在面包篮里。|一群驳船船员在争论天气。}
# en: A low-beamed tavern with small windows, a fire that never goes out and a landlady polishing glasses behind the bar.
scene [062fe7] = 低矮梁柱的酒馆，小小的窗户，炉火永不熄灭，老板娘在吧台后擦杯子。
# en: A hot supper
opt.supper.label [5ef676] = 一顿热晚饭
# en: Health and Mood; it ends a hungry month.
opt.supper.hint [dd3967] = 健康和心情；能结束挨饿的一个月。
# en: {Stew, bread, an apple you didn't ask for. You leave warm all the way through.|The landlady watches you eat as if she'd been worried about you. Perhaps she had.|You finish the bowl and she fills it again without asking. "Growing," she says, though you're not.}
opt.supper.say.1 [fe473d] = {炖菜、面包，还有一个你没要的苹果。你从里暖到外地离开。|老板娘看着你吃，好像一直在担心你。也许真是。|你吃完一碗，她没问就又盛满了。“长身体呢，”她说，虽然你早就不长了。}
# en: Buy a round for the table
opt.round.label [d861a8] = 请全桌喝一轮
# en: Renown; the regulars will remember.
opt.round.hint [bcc9a8] = 声望；常客们会记得。
# en: {The regulars lift their cups to you. One of them, very drunk, makes a speech about students.|"To the castle!" someone shouts, and the whole room drinks to it, and to you.|The barge crew drink your health and then argue about whether you're a good sort. They decide you are.}
opt.round.say.1 [9eeb04] = {常客们向你举杯。其中一个醉得厉害，发表了一通关于学生的演讲。|“为城堡干杯！”有人喊道，满屋子人都为城堡、也为你喝了一杯。|驳船船员们祝你健康，然后争论你算不算个好人。结论是算。}
# en: A cup of cider
opt.cider.label [26847e] = 一杯苹果酒
# en: A little Mood.
opt.cider.hint [26b71f] = 少许心情。
# en: {Cold, sharp and tasting of last autumn's apples.|You drink it by the window and watch the lake turn gold.|The cat in the bread basket opens one eye at you and closes it again.}
opt.cider.say.1 [fc5417] = {冰凉、清冽，有去年秋天苹果的味道。|你在窗边喝着，看湖面变成金色。|面包篮里的猫睁开一只眼睛看看你，又闭上了。}
# en: Just warm your hands at the fire
opt.look.label [65a973] = 只在炉火边暖暖手
# en: {Nobody minds. The fire never goes out; that's the point of it.|You sit by the fire until your hands remember they're hands.|The landlady leaves you be. Sometimes that's the service.}
opt.look.say.1 [d0f115] = {没人介意。炉火永不熄灭，就是为了这个。|你在炉火边坐到双手想起自己是手。|老板娘没打扰你。有时候这就是服务。}

@event offer_ashwood_wand
# en: Prove It
title [ef8e7a] = 证明给我看
# en: Under a cloth at the back of Mir's stall is an ashwood duelling wand, dense and dark. "It bites anything that blocks it," says Mir. "I'm not selling it to just anyone. Show me you can hold it, and it's yours, for what the ash cost me."
text [f6f4c9] = 米尔摊子后面的布底下，有一根白蜡木决斗魔杖，沉实而黝黑。“谁挡它，它就咬谁，”米尔说，“我不随便卖。证明你拿得住它，它就归你，价钱就是白蜡木的成本。”
# en: A market stall with a single dark wand on a velvet cloth, an artificer student holding a hand over it protectively.
scene [147e14] = 集市摊位上，天鹅绒布上只放着一根深色魔杖，一个做奇械的学生护着它。
# en: Leave it under its cloth
opt.left.label [ef3629] = 让它留在布底下
# en: Mir covers it again, relieved. "It'd probably bite me too."
opt.left.say.1 [d7954d] = 米尔又把它盖好，松了口气。“它大概也会咬我。”
# en: Pay up, and prove it
opt.right.label [8f8d0e] = 付钱，证明给他看
# en: A dear price, handed back if it won't answer you. A wand for fights: anything that blocks it takes a jolt.
opt.right.hint [017731] = 价钱不菲，它不认你就退钱。战斗用魔杖：谁挡它，谁就挨一下。
# en: The wand jumps in your hand like a live thing and a spark cracks off the well. Mir whoops. "It likes you! Probably."
opt.right.say.1 [05d962] = 魔杖在你手里像活物一样一跳，一道火花从井沿上炸开。米尔欢呼起来。“它喜欢你！大概吧。”
# en: The wand sulks in your hand and won't so much as spark. Mir gives you your money back, kindly, which is worse.
opt.right.say.2 [62df5c] = 魔杖在你手里闹脾气，连个火星都不冒。米尔客气地把钱退给你，这更难受。

@event offer_ward_cloak
# en: Ward Thread
title [29797d] = 护界线
# en: The tailor beckons you into her back room. On the table is a spool of thread that shines faintly when you aren't looking at it. "Sister Amaranth sent it down. Ward thread. She says you're to have a cloak with it, if you can pay for the hemming. Fire and frost slide off it like rain."
text [b3e0cd] = 裁缝招手让你进里屋。桌上有一轴线，你不看它的时候，它会微微发光。“阿玛兰斯修女送下来的。护界线。她说要给你做一件斗篷，只要你付得起缝边的钱。火和霜会像雨水一样从上面滑走。”
# en: A tailor's back room, a spool of faintly shining thread on the table, a grey cloak half-hemmed beside it.
scene [9b8cd6] = 裁缝的里屋，桌上一轴微微发光的线，旁边一件缝了一半边的灰斗篷。
# en: You can't afford a cloak
opt.left.label [3833e6] = 你买不起斗篷
# en: The tailor puts the spool away in a drawer marked YOURS. "It'll keep," she says.
opt.left.say.1 [4c4177] = 裁缝把那轴线收进一个写着“你的”的抽屉。“放得住，”她说。
# en: Have the cloak made
opt.right.label [fb8f9d] = 请她做斗篷
# en: A robe for fights: more Health, and spells of fire, frost and starlight hit softer.
opt.right.hint [491fd9] = 战斗用长袍：更多生命，火焰、冰霜和星光的法术打得更轻。
# en: She hems it in an afternoon, muttering. When you put it on, the thread warms, and the draught from the door stops at your collar.
opt.right.say.1 [a90063] = 她一个下午就缝好了，嘴里嘟嘟囔囔。你穿上时，线温热起来，门口的冷风停在了你的衣领处。

@event offer_pocket_almanac
# en: The Lighthouse Page
title [a33e7f] = 灯塔那一页
# en: On Grimsby's counter is a pocket almanac: fifty years of tides and moons, every margin full of his own pencil notes. You reach for it and he moves it, gently, out of reach. "Not for sale," he says. "Well. Not for sale to someone who doesn't know what it's for."
text [0a69e2] = 格林斯比的柜台上有一本袖珍年历：五十年的潮汐和月相，每一页的页边都写满了他的铅笔批注。你伸手去拿，他轻轻地把它挪开了。“非卖品，”他说，“嗯。不卖给不知道它有什么用的人。”
# en: An old bookseller holding a tiny thick book out of reach, its margins crowded with pencil notes.
scene [e6b8ee] = 一位老书商把一本又小又厚的书举在够不着的地方，页边挤满了铅笔批注。
# en: Leave him his almanac
opt.left.label [c7df99] = 把年历留给他
# en: He tucks it back in his waistcoat pocket and pats it. "Thank you," he says, oddly formal.
opt.left.say.1 [e70ebd] = 他把它塞回背心口袋，拍了拍。“谢谢你，”他说，客气得有点奇怪。
# en: {knows(grimsby.lighthouses): Talk to him about lighthouses|Argue that you'd use it}
opt.right.label [8f7876] = {knows(grimsby.lighthouses): 和他聊灯塔|说服他你会用它}
# en: {knows(grimsby.lighthouses): You know what he loves.|A negotiation.} A pocket almanac: tides, moons and weather on the right cards.
opt.right.hint [995f75] = {knows(grimsby.lighthouses): 你知道他爱什么。|一场交涉。}袖珍年历：在合适的卡牌上查潮汐、月相和天气。
# en: You ask him about the lighthouse at the point and he talks for an hour. At the end he presses the almanac into your hands for a few coins. "Page forty," he says. "That's the good one."
opt.right.say.1 [43013d] = 你问起海角上的灯塔，他一说就是一个小时。最后他只收了几个硬币，把年历塞到你手里。“第四十页，”他说，“那页最好。”
# en: You tell him what you'd look up first: the next spring tide, the next new moon. He considers this for a long time. "Yes," he says at last, and sells it to you.
opt.right.say.2 [2ba27d] = 你告诉他你会先查什么：下一次大潮，下一次新月。他想了很久。“好吧，”他终于说，把它卖给了你。
# en: "No, no," he says kindly, "you'd look up the weather and nothing else." He's right, and that's the worst of it.
opt.right.say.3 [bbdf4e] = “不，不，”他和气地说，“你只会查天气。”他说得对，这才最糟。

@event offer_measuring_spoon
# en: Measure Twice
title [8b97fb] = 量两遍
# en: Old Pell is holding up a brass spoon worn thin on one side. "Forty years," he says. "It's never been wrong. I'm getting a new one." He sets six vials in front of you. "Measure these. If you count right, it's yours, for what the brass is worth."
text [6c08a1] = 老佩尔举着一把一侧磨薄了的黄铜勺。“四十年，”他说，“从没错过。我要换把新的了。”他在你面前摆了六个小瓶。“量这些。数对了，它就归你，按黄铜的价钱。”
# en: An old apothecary holding a thin brass spoon up to the light, a row of empty vials in front of a student.
scene [f9f936] = 一位老药剂师把一把细细的黄铜勺举到亮处，学生面前摆着一排空瓶。
# en: Not today
opt.left.label [479f6f] = 今天不了
# en: He shrugs and puts the spoon in his waistcoat pocket. "It'll wait. Spoons are patient."
opt.left.say.1 [d9900d] = 他耸耸肩，把勺子放进背心口袋。“它等得起。勺子有耐心。”
# en: Count the drops aloud
opt.right.label [80f706] = 大声数药滴
# en: Money down, handed back if you miscount. A spoon for brewing cards.
opt.right.hint [3cc148] = 先付钱，数错了就退。一把用于调制卡牌的勺子。
# en: You count aloud, every drop, and every vial is right. Pell says nothing for a long moment. Then: "Measure twice," and hands you the spoon.
opt.right.say.1 [05ae35] = 你大声数着，每一滴都数，每一瓶都对。佩尔好半天没说话。然后：“量两遍。”他把勺子递给了你。
# en: You lose count in the fifth vial. Pell hands your money back. "Count aloud," he says. "Every time. Then come back."
opt.right.say.2 [b23077] = 你在第五瓶数乱了。佩尔把钱退给你。“大声数，”他说，“每一次都要。然后再来。”

@event offer_honey_tin
# en: A Tin of Silver
title [1674d1] = 一罐银色
# en: Maud is at the hives, veil down, lifting out a frame of comb that shines like poured silver. "Silver bees," she says. "They don't take to everyone. They've taken to you, dearie. Help me with the frames and there's a tin in it."
text [8b654f] = 莫德在蜂箱边，放下面纱，提起一框亮得像倒出来的银子一样的蜂巢。“银蜂，”她说，“它们不是谁都亲近。它们亲近你，亲爱的。帮我搬巢框，就送你一罐。”
# en: A thatched cottage's garden full of beehives, an old woman in a veil lifting a frame of silver comb.
scene [67ecd4] = 茅草小屋的花园里摆满蜂箱，一个戴面纱的老妇人正提起一框银色的蜂巢。
# en: Keep well back from the bees
opt.left.label [0b8fbf] = 离蜜蜂远远的
# en: Maud laughs and does it herself. A silver bee follows you to the gate anyway, curious.
opt.left.say.1 [f9e219] = 莫德笑着自己干了。一只银蜂还是好奇地跟你到了门口。
# en: Help with the frames
opt.right.label [f22555] = 帮忙搬巢框
# en: A tin of honey: a way to sweeten someone on the right cards.
opt.right.hint [1431a0] = 一罐蜂蜜：在合适的卡牌上给人甜头。
# en: You get stung once, politely, on the thumb. Maud fills a dented tin with silver honey and presses it into your hands. "Share it," she says. "That's what it's for."
opt.right.say.1 [978366] = 你被礼貌地蛰了一下拇指。莫德往一只磕瘪的罐子里装满银色的蜂蜜，塞到你手里。“分给别人，”她说，“它就是干这个用的。”
